+    "text": "A run's checkpoint hash is train.state_sha256 of the trained model (for arm L the LoRA-wrapped model, base weights and adapters; N's is the loaded base model's). It is not a file-byte hash. Computation: h = SHA-256(); for each key k of module.state_dict() in sorted order (Python string order), with t = the tensor detached, moved to the CPU and made contiguous: h.update(UTF-8 bytes of k + b'\\0' + str(t.dtype) + b'\\0' + str(tuple(t.shape)) + b'\\0'), then h.update(the raw bytes of t, flattened and viewed as uint8, in the host's byte order); the hash is h.hexdigest() (64 lowercase hex). TEST evaluation recomputes it on the model loaded from the saved checkpoint and requires equality with the freeze record (through the TEST marker) before the model is evaluated.",
